 ## Key Design Decisions
 
 - **Commands over HTTPS, one authoritative board per event.** Editors submit commands to the server, which assigns each committed edit one event revision. Peer-to-peer or browser-side merging was rejected: the tenets require one authoritative revision regardless of delivery route, and offline editing is a non-goal.
+- **Self-hosted WebSockets for change delivery.** Chosen over five-second HTTPS polling (stateless and simplest, but repeated reads and several seconds of lag) and a hosted realtime service (least connection operations, but recurring fees and provider coupling). Fast updates without a realtime vendor outweigh the added connection-capacity and reconnect work. All three options could meet the 15-second goal, so the choice rests on latency and vendor independence, not feasibility. Criteria, per-option analysis, and downstream obligations: `docs/decisions/change-delivery-transport.md`.
